From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 22:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Audio: clear pending MAT output on passthrough codec reset

A passthrough codec reset clears parser input and timestamps but leaves the
MAT packer's partial packet, completed output queue and timing state alive.
A seek can consequently mix pre-reset payload or timing into later output.

Add an explicit MAT reset that clears every state field and both output
buffers, then invoke it from the existing codec reset. Retain the packer
object: its creation currently depends on the TrueHD staging buffer being
empty, so deleting only the packer would not reliably recreate it.

After reset the packer waits for a new major sync and produces the same
bytes as a fresh packer fed the new stream. This does not change seamless
branch handling during continuous playback or implement resume preroll.
Native tests compare the production packer against a fresh instance after
partial/queued output and across sample-rate and timing discontinuities.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/PackerMAT.cpp b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/PackerMAT.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/PackerMAT.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/PackerMAT.cpp
@@ -147,6 +147,14 @@
   m_buffer.reserve(MAT_BUFFER_SIZE);
 }
 
+void CPackerMAT::Reset()
+{
+  m_state = {};
+  m_bufferCount = 0;
+  m_buffer.clear();
+  m_outputQueue.clear();
+}
+
 // On a high level, a MAT frame consists of a sequence of padded TrueHD frames
 // The size of the padded frame can be determined from the frame time/sequence code in the frame header,
 // since it varies to accommodate spikes in bitrate.
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/PackerMAT.h b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/PackerMAT.h
--- a/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/PackerMAT.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/AudioEngine/Utils/PackerMAT.h
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 
   bool PackTrueHD(const uint8_t* data, int size);
   std::vector<uint8_t> GetOutputFrame();
+  void Reset();
 
 private:
   struct MATState
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Audio/DVDAudioCodecPassthrough.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Audio/DVDAudioCodecPassthrough.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Audio/DVDAudioCodecPassthrough.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Audio/DVDAudioCodecPassthrough.cpp
@@ -302,6 +302,8 @@
   m_currentPts = DVD_NOPTS_VALUE;
   m_nextPts = DVD_NOPTS_VALUE;
   m_parser.Reset();
+  if (m_packerMAT)
+    m_packerMAT->Reset();
 }
 
 int CDVDAudioCodecPassthrough::GetBufferSize()
